        "original_id": "e2ce5133-3eda-53eb-84f6-6011e2a1094c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Warlock in Spite of Himself, Le Médecin malgré lui\n- People: Molière, Jean-Baptiste Poquelin\n- Topics: title references, French comedy\n\nFacts:\n- Molière was the stage name of Jean-Baptiste Poquelin, a French playwright and actor born on 15 January 1622 and died on 17 February 1673.\n- Molière is considered one of the greatest masters of comedy in Western literature.\n- Le Médecin malgré lui is a work by Molière whose title translates as \"The Doctor, in Spite of Himself.\"\n- The title of The Warlock in Spite of Himself is a play on the title of Molière's Le Médecin malgré lui.",
